course: dictionary
lesson: 2542
title: A defender keeps things safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A defender is a person who protects someone or something from attack or harm. Read the clues around the word: «Picture a castle under siege: the attackers waited for weeks until the defenders ran out of food.» Attackers try to get in, and defenders keep them out. So defenders are on the side that protects.
explain: Defender also has a sports meaning. In football, hockey and netball, defenders stay back near their own goal to stop the other team from scoring. «In soccer, an attacker is offside if they are behind the last defender.» Here a defender is a player in the team, not a person in a castle.
explain: The word can also mean someone who speaks up for an idea or for another person. Standing up for a friend who is being bullied makes you a defender, or an upstander. To check your meaning, swap in "protector" for "defender". If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: A defender is a person who protects someone or something from attack or harm.
fact: In team sports, a defender is a player whose job is to stop the other team from scoring.
fact: Phrases you may see: «a strong defender», «defenders of the castle», «left defender», «right defender».
fact: Someone who speaks up for an idea or for another person is also a defender.
fact: The opposite side in a castle story is the attackers, and in a game it is the other team's attackers.
exercise: «The defenders of the castle kept the enemy out for months.» Who are the defenders? | The people who attack the castle | *The people who protect the castle from attack | The cooks who make the meals | The visitors who come to see the castle
exercise: In netball, what is a defender's job? | To score as many goals as possible | *To stop the other team from scoring | To sit on the bench | To referee the game
exercise: «He was a strong defender of his little brother.» What does defender mean here? | A person who wears armour | Someone who is always fighting with him | A player who scores goals | *Someone who protects and stands up for him
test: In «Picture a castle under siege: the attackers waited for weeks until the defenders ran out of food», which word is on the opposite side to the defenders? | Weeks | Castle | *Attackers | Food
test: Ella sees a boy being bullied and steps in to help him. What is Ella? | A goalkeeper | *A defender, or upstander | A visitor | A referee
exam: In «In soccer, an attacker is offside if they are behind the last defender», what is the defender trying to do? | Pass the ball backwards | *Stop attackers getting past | Score a goal | Leave the pitch
